{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The family of the Hanochi.</b> Because the nations would disparage them and say: What are these tracing their lineage by their tribes? Do they think the Egyptians did not have their way with their mothers? If they ruled over their bodies, how much more so over their wives! Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, cast His name upon them — a heh on this side and a yod on this side — to declare: I testify concerning them that they are the sons of their fathers. And this is what is expounded through David (Psalms 122): ״שִׁבְטֵי יָהּ עֵדוּת לְיִשְׂרָאֵל״ — this name testifies concerning them to their tribes. Therefore in all of them He wrote הַחֲנֹכִי, הַפַּלֻּאִי, but in Yimna there was no need to say ״מִשְׁפַּחַת הַיִּמְנִי״ because the name is fixed in it — a yod at the beginning and a heh at the end (Yalkut Shimoni)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:50.558998183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}